    content:
      "Chicken Tikka Masala pairs yogurt-marinated, flame-charred chicken with a spiced, buttery tomato and cream sauce that is rich but not heavy.\n\n### Ingredients:\n\n**For the chicken:**\n\n* 700 g boneless, skinless chicken thighs, cut into 4 cm pieces\n* 150 g full-fat plain yogurt\n* 1 tbsp (15 ml) lemon juice\n* 2 garlic cloves, finely grated\n* 2 cm piece fresh ginger, finely grated\n* 2 tsp (10 ml) garam masala\n* 1 tsp (5 ml) Kashmiri chilli powder\n* 1/2 tsp (2.5 ml) ground turmeric\n* 1 tsp (5 ml) salt\n* 1 tbsp (15 ml) neutral oil\n\n**For the masala sauce:**\n\n* 2 tbsp (30 g) ghee or butter\n* 1 large onion (about 200 g), finely chopped\n* 3 garlic cloves, finely grated\n* 3 cm piece fresh ginger, finely grated\n* 1 green chilli, finely chopped\n* 2 tsp (10 ml) garam masala\n* 1 tsp (5 ml) ground cumin\n* 1 tsp (5 ml) ground coriander\n* 1 tsp (5 ml) Kashmiri chilli powder\n* 400 g tomato passata\n* 150 ml single (light) cream\n* 1 tsp (5 ml) sugar\n* 1 tsp (5 ml) dried fenugreek leaves (kasuri methi), crushed\n* 3/4 tsp (4 ml) salt\n* Small handful fresh coriander, chopped\n\n### Instructions:\n\n1. Mix all the chicken ingredients except the oil in a bowl and leave to marinate for 15 minutes while you start the sauce.\n2. Melt the ghee in a 28 cm deep frying pan or casserole over medium heat. Add the onion and cook for 8–10 minutes, stirring, until soft and golden.\n3. Add the garlic, ginger and green chilli and cook for 1 minute until fragrant, then stir in the ground spices and cook for 30 seconds without letting them burn.\n4. Pour in the passata, add the sugar and salt, and simmer gently, partly covered, for 12–15 minutes until thickened and the oil starts to separate at the edges.\n5. Meanwhile, heat the oven grill to its highest setting (about 250°C). Line a baking tray with foil, brush with the oil, and spread the chicken out in a single layer.\n6. Grill the chicken 8–10 cm from the element for 8–10 minutes, turning once, until charred in spots and cooked through to an internal temperature of 74°C.\n7. Blend the sauce with a stick blender until smooth (optional, for a restaurant-style finish), then stir in the cream and fenugreek leaves.\n8. Add the grilled chicken and any juices to the sauce and simmer for 3–4 minutes to let the flavours meld. Taste and adjust salt.\n9. Scatter with fresh coriander and serve with basmati rice or naan.\n\n### Tips:\n\n* For deeper flavour, marinate the chicken for up to 24 hours in the fridge.\n* Chicken thighs stay juicier than breast; if using breast, reduce grilling time by 2–3 minutes.\n* The curry keeps for 3 days in the fridge and freezes well for up to 3 months.",
